																		Sir Reginald
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/eagleknight9" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6538548); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6538548&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609991286" alt="EagleKnight9" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6538548)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/eagleknight9" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6538548); return false;" >EagleKnight9</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608240076 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Dec 2020 21:21</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847222">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Action/Psychological</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Has several non-Foundation documents in the beginning, such as interview logs conducted by non-Foundation personnel. Has several notes/'diary' entries written by Sir Reginald scattered throughout the article to progress the narrative. Logs of interview/therapy sessions towards the end of the article.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The SCP is a reality anomaly that has the ability to transfer fictional characters into the base SCP universe based on the degree to which the residents in the SCP universe believe that the character exists.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The SCP first manifests as &quot;Sir Reginald,&quot; a protagonist in a kid's show. The entity (SCP-1) has no memory of it's life prior to its manifestation.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>SCP-1 is not originally aware that it is a fictional character, with the police arresting him.</p>
<p>He is questioned and then put in a mental asylum due to his strange mannerisms. The questioner assumes SCP-1 is roleplaying as Sir Reginald and mentions it. SCP-1 slowly regains some memories and breaks out.</p>
<p>During his escape, he stopped to watch his show through a window, he regains all of his memories. The Foundation finds him in front of the window, sobbing.</p>
<p>SCP-1 tries to live like he's in his reality, so it seems like he is trying to live in two worlds simultaneously, degrading his mental state.</p>
<p>SCP-1 is labeled as a SCP due to his anomalous intellect and behavior. The Foundation assumes that SCP-1 is Sir Reginald.</p>
<p>Sir Reginald is watching the TV, when he sees himself in the frame<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-437809-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-437809-1')">1</a></sup>. 1 stares at 2, asking who 2 is. 2 says that he's the same person as 1. 1 says that he doesn't know who 2 is, saying that 2 might look like him, but that 2 was different. 1 then says that 2 should stop pretending that he was 1, and that 2 is missing the point. 1 then asks, <em>&quot;what are you really?&quot;</em></p>
<p>Sir Reginald has some profound questions, and is struggling to find answers. <em>Is he human? Does he have a purpose? Is he real?</em></p>
<p>Sir Reginald realizes that life has the meaning that he assigns to it, so he finds meaning in helping the Foundation. He helps contain reality anomalies.</p>
<p>The article ends with 2 telling 1 that although they look alike, he isn't the same person as 1, and he is content with that. 1 smiles at 2 and says that he thinks he's finally starting to recognize 2 again.</p>
<p><strong>Hook:</strong> The premise of a SCP slowly losing its mind due to it being foreign to the universe, but late finding purpose.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
<p>Shortened article to meet limit, many details are missing from previous revisions.</p>
<p><strong>Edit Announcements</strong></p>
<p>Edit 12/18: Made the SCP an effect rather than a specific entity, with the SCP no longer having a tendency to create anomalous weaponry and can no longer possess people.</p>
<p>Edit 1/4: Rewrote most of the Central Narrative portion to try to compensate for the inconsistencies pointed out in caspain2's post.</p>
<p>Edit 1/5: Rewrote most of the ending of the Central Narrative as a response to Grigori's suggestions.</p>
<p>Edit 1/6: Rewrote some of the end of the Central Narrative as a response to caspian2's suggestions and shortened the text.</p>
</div>
