<p>Hello hello! Not an official critter here, but I can still read and give opinions.<br />
So, I mostly agree with Grigori above. The idea is really cool, I personally love this kind of 'meta' stuff. But I would also recommend cutting out the anomalous weapon bit. I don't think the possession is a problem myself, it makes sense as a way for a fictional character to 'anchor' itself to our reality; but I think the anomalous weapons bit would simply make it look as though you're making it be more dangerous than it needs to be.<br />
Not everything needs to be able to destroy a plane to be interesting.</p>
<p>This aside, I believe, another interesting concept you could explore instead- if you think the personal woes of Sir Reginald coming to terms with not being &quot;real&quot; are not enough- is how they got here at all, if that is still an active phenomenon/it can spread to other media, and what that means for whatever work Reginald is from originally.<br />
Just a bunch of ideas, you're free to completely disregard them if you don't feel they're interesting enough for you.</p>
<p>Overall though, I really like this! Definitely gonna be reading it once it's written out as a draft and hopefully as a real Object!</p>

